@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Content-bank image ingestion (CON-281). All requests require authentication —
# run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http first. Needs image-service running
# (default `docker compose up`) and GEMINI_API_KEY (vision + embedding).
#
# Accepted: JPEG, PNG, WebP, GIF, HEIC/HEIF, AVIF, TIFF, BMP (operator cap,
# default 50 MB). SVG is rejected (code=vector_rejected). Uploads are
# deduplicated within the tenant by checksum.
#
# The asset lands as type=IMG, status=pending; image-service normalizes,
# EXIF-strips, classifies, extracts regions, describes, and writes alt text
# asynchronously → ready / partial / failed. content = the description;
# alt_text = the generated alt text (never overwrites a user edit).
#
# Fixture: ../images/sample.png.

### Upload an image  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ../images/sample.png
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("imgAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### Extraction + region blocks (poll)  [protected]
# extraction.status → complete | partial | failed, with failure_code/failure_reason.
# Each block has a normalized bbox anchor.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}/image
Accept: application/json

### Asset — description in content, alt_text, normalized_url on file  [protected]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}
Accept: application/json

### Chunks: description + one per region (CON-312)  [protected]
# source_label "Image description" / "Region N"; region chunks carry the bbox.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}/chunks
Accept: application/json

### Edit the description — re-embeds it and keeps the region chunks (CON-312)  [protected]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "sample",
  "content": "A bar chart of monthly revenue, peaking in March."
}

### Echo the stored alt text back — alt_text_edited_by_user stays false (CON-312)  [protected]
# Replace the value with the asset's current alt_text to see the flag not flip.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "sample",
  "content": "A bar chart of monthly revenue, peaking in March.",
  "alt_text": "<current alt_text>"
}

### Set alt text by hand — flips alt_text_edited_by_user=true  [protected]
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "sample",
  "content": "A bar chart of monthly revenue, peaking in March.",
  "alt_text": "Bar chart: monthly revenue, highest in March"
}

### Regenerate alt text (sync; overwrites even a hand edit)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}/image/alt-text

### Re-extract, optionally pinning the extract model  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}/image/reextract
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gemini-2.5-pro"
}

### Manual first run — only when the upload didn't enqueue (409 if a run exists)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}/image/extract

### Upload an SVG (expects failed, code=vector_rejected)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="logo.svg"
Content-Type: image/svg+xml

<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10"><rect width="10" height="10"/></svg>
--boundary--

### Delete the image asset  [protected]
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/{{imgAssetId}}
